  scope-exclusion-bullets-become-absence-obligations
    [other] scope-exclusion-bullets-become-absence-obligations/positive-wording-not-enforced-in-code
      The description wording of an exclusion obligation is still chosen by the model. The only change that targets it is prompt text with one worked example. Nothing in code checks or forces the negative form. A bullet with a trailing explanatory clause can still come out as 'The change excludes X from Y', which is work to perform. The new code sets only `satisfied_by_absence`, `required_evidence` and the coverage marker. None of these alters the description.
