    [other] scope-exclusion-same-evidence-same-status/decomposer-still-may-split-or-miscategorize-exclusion
      The prompt change tells the decomposer to read past a trailing explanatory clause, but nothing enforces that. A bullet can still yield a positive obligation, or a clause can be split into a separate obligation. Whether that obligation is marked as an exclusion depends on the requirement's section. A clause split off or filed under a different section would carry no scope-exclusion mark and would be judged as work to do, diverging from its siblings.
